# See core/deb/shlibs.local for the general mechanism this project already
# established for core, and core/deb-3rdparty-drivers/shlibs.local for the
# fuller writeup of the same finding applied to a consumer of a private
# library it does not itself ship. Same reasoning here: the compiled
# _PyIndi*.so extension links libindiclient.so.2 via RPATH
# (pyindi-client/deb/rules), indi-stable-core-libs ships no shlibs file of
# its own (dh_makeshlibs deliberately skipped, "do not advertise a private
# library system-wide"), and indi-stable-core-libs is already installed on
# the build host as a Build-Depends -- so dpkg-shlibdeps finds the real file
# through RPATH but has no dependency information for it without this file.
#
# Bare package name, no version relation -- shlibs entries take literal text
# only, so a version here would go stale silently on every release (same
# reasoning as core/deb/shlibs.local and
# core/deb-3rdparty-drivers/shlibs.local).
libindiclient 2 indi-stable-core-libs
